### Use Case Explanation

**Actor:** User (single user, no authentication)

**Use Cases (mapped to menu options):**

| # | Use Case | Menu Option | Description |
|---|----------|-------------|-------------|
| UC1 | Add Expense | 1 | Record new expense with date, amount, category, description |
| UC2 | View Expenses | 2 | List all expenses in formatted table with totals |
| UC3 | Update Expense | 3 | Modify existing expense (date, amount, category, description) |
| UC4 | Delete Expense | 4 | Remove expense with confirmation |
| UC5 | Add Income | 5 | Record income with source, amount, date, description |
| UC6 | View Income | 6 | List all income records in formatted table |
| UC7 | Update Income | 7 | Modify existing income record |
| UC8 | Delete Income | 8 | Remove income with confirmation |
| UC9 | Manage Budget | 9 | Set/view/delete monthly budgets, see usage % |
| UC10 | View Financial Summary | 10 | Overall income, expenses, balance, counts |
| UC11 | Generate Reports | 11 | Category reports, monthly, analytics, trends |
| UC12 | Search/Filter Transactions | 12 | Filter by type, category, date, amount, keyword |
| UC13 | Export Data | 13 | Export to CSV (all, expenses, income, by month) |
| UC14 | View Help | 14 | Built-in help documentation |
| UC15 | Exit Application | 0 | Clean shutdown |

**Relationships:**
- **Include (..>)**: Base use case includes another (e.g., Add Expense includes View Expenses for selection)
- **Extend (..>)**: Optional extension (e.g., Update Expense extends View Expenses - you view first, then choose to update)

**Not Modeled (Out of Scope):**
- Multi-user, authentication, cloud sync, recurring transactions, GUI, API